            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Intersect the graph with the perpendicular through A.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "The shortest distance is perpendicular to the line, so $AP$ has gradient $-\\frac13$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y-2&=-\\frac13(x-4)\\\\3y-6&=-x+4\\\\x+3y&=10\\end{align*}$$\n\nAt the intersection with $y=3x$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x+3(3x)&=10\\\\10x&=10\\\\x&=1\\\\y&=3(1)\\\\y&=3\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, $P(1,3)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 94
  },
